sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Fund Admin
    participant SOM as Sell Offer Management Subsystem
    participant TEN as Tenant Management Subsystem
    participant BAL as Balance Crediting / Debiting Subsystem
    participant RT as Real-time Sync (SignalR)
    actor Viewers as Traders viewing the pair

    Note over Admin,Viewers: PHASE 1 - WITHDRAWAL
    Note over Admin,Viewers: Every state change below is also emitted as an audit event to the Audit subsystem, asynchronously and off the trade path

    Admin->>SOM: Withdraw offer (offerId, idempotency key)
    SOM->>TEN: Authorize (user, role, tenant status)
    alt Not authorized
        TEN-->>SOM: Denied
        SOM-->>Admin: Rejected NOT_AUTHORIZED
    else Authorized
        TEN-->>SOM: Allowed
        SOM->>SOM: Request withdrawal (offerId, reason)
        SOM->>SOM: Atomic lock: insert lock record (fencing token = lock version, expiration)
        alt Offer is locked
            SOM-->>SOM: Rejected OFFER_LOCKED with retryAfter
            SOM-->>Admin: Cannot withdraw now, offer is being purchased (retryAfter)
        else Offer already executed, withdrawn or expired
            SOM-->>SOM: Rejected OFFER_NOT_AVAILABLE
            SOM-->>Admin: Nothing to withdraw (current status)
        else Withdrawn
            SOM-)RT: OfferStateChanged (Withdrawn, version)
            RT-)Viewers: Offer removed from all screens
            SOM-->>SOM: Withdrawn
            SOM->>BAL: Release hold on the block (idempotent)
            BAL-->>SOM: Released
            SOM->>SOM: Offer status Withdrawn
            SOM-->>Admin: Offer withdrawn
        end
    end

    Note over SOM,BAL: If the hold release fails, the Hold Timeout Sweeper retries it, so funds are never stranded

    Note over Admin,Viewers: PHASE 2 - EXPIRY (time-in-force)

    loop Expiry sweeper, every tick
        SOM->>SOM: Find Published offers past their expiry time
        SOM->>SOM: Request expiry (offerId)
        SOM->>SOM: Atomic expire, only if state is Available (version+1)
        alt Offer is locked
            SOM-->>SOM: Rejected OFFER_LOCKED
            Note over SOM: Expiry is never forced. The purchase outcome wins and expiry is retried on the next tick
        else Offer already executed, withdrawn or expired
            SOM-->>SOM: Rejected OFFER_NOT_AVAILABLE
        else Expired
            SOM-)RT: OfferStateChanged (Expired, version)
            RT-)Viewers: Offer removed from all screens
            SOM-->>SOM: Expired
            SOM->>BAL: Release hold on the block (idempotent)
            BAL-->>SOM: Released
            SOM->>SOM: Offer status Expired
            SOM-)Admin: Notification: offer expired
        end
    end

    Note over SOM,BAL: Pre-Paid but expired - ledger entries are released by a timeout, so a crash cannot strand funds